window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"singed","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Singed","Singed","Locke","Singed"],"spikes":[{"when":"Level 2","text":"The lane starts hinging on your Fling — every trade he dodges it, he wins; every one he eats it, you win."},{"when":"Level 3","text":"Mega Adhesive grounds Ashen Pursuit — his only escape, flat 10s cooldown."},{"when":"Locke first item","text":"Purgatory starts executing your low-HP poison retreats — stop limping away half-dead."},{"when":"Two-plus items","text":"Your tanky run-it-down style neutralises his single-target burst — even again."}],"wants":{"you":["Fling landed on his commit, not on cooldown","Poison ticks stacked while he chases","Retreats started at healthy HP after his 6"],"foe":["Your Fling baited and side-stepped","A low-HP retreat to execute with Purgatory","Single-target burst landed before your tank arrives"]},"early":"Your poison trades into his 950-range nails, and level 2 onward hinges on whether he dodges Fling. The real lever is Mega Adhesive: it grounds Ashen Pursuit, his only mobility on a flat 10s, so hold the goo for his step-up and he is stuck in the cloud with no exit.","mid":"At 6 Insanity Potion's Grievous Wounds cuts the heal-back at the end of Soul Ignition, so his self-damage sticks. Break one habit though: Purgatory executes low-HP poison retreats, and Silver Stake hits harder the lower you are. Leave fights at an HP line his execute cannot reach.","late":"With items the matchup evens back out for good: your tanky run-it-down style neutralises his single-target burst, and he cannot execute a Singed who manages his health bar. Run his team over in fights, Fling his carry into yours, and keep the retreat discipline — that is the entire matchup late.","whys":["Level 1 is even — your poison trades evenly against his on-hit poke.","At 2 the lane hinges on whether he dodges your Fling, not on raw stats.","Level 3 stays even: your Mega Adhesive setups balance his Q burst.","Through 4-5 Mega Adhesive grounds his only dash — Fling then roots him in it.","At 6 Insanity Potion's Grievous Wounds guts the Soul Ignition heal-back.","His first item makes Purgatory execute your low-HP poison retreats — his one clear stage.","With items your tanky run-it-down style beats his single-target burst — you win outright."]});
