window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"singed","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Zaahen","Skill","Skill","Skill","Singed","Singed"],"spikes":[{"when":"Zaahen level 2","text":"Glaive recast knocks you up and Aureate Rush is percent-health — give the wave, keep your HP."},{"when":"Level 3","text":"Mega Adhesive grounds Aureate Rush, his only dash on 10s — the lane steadies."},{"when":"Your first item","text":"Poison itemization plus your level lead from tempo tilt the lane your way."},{"when":"Two-plus items","text":"Grievous Wounds on Poison Trail cuts his Glaive and ult heals — attrition is yours."}],"wants":{"you":["Tempo through proxying and quick backs","Goo held for his Aureate Rush dash","A level lead built while he pushes air"],"foe":["A level-2 all-in you stand still for","Farming denied without his tempo answer","Dreaded Return pulling you back mid-run"]},"early":"Level 1 is a pure farming check, but respect his level-2 spike: The Darkin Glaive slashes twice, heals him, and recasts into a knockup, so give ground rather than blood. From 3 the goo grounds Aureate Rush — his only dash, 10s at rank 1 — and through 4-5 you run the tempo loop: proxy, farm, run.","mid":"At 6 a straight duel is a wash, but Insanity Potion's Grievous Wounds bites both his heals — The Darkin Glaive and Grim Deliverance. Your first item is the tilt. The one ability that beats running is Dreaded Return: an 850-range pull on 14s that drags you back, so break the line before you commit to the run.","late":"With two-plus items you are the stronger threat: kiting means he never finishes you, and Fling turns his own engage into a death sentence. But Cultivation of War lets him revive once Determination fills, so never spend your ultimate on that kill until the bar is empty — split, drag him out, and Fling him into your team.","whys":["Level 1 is a skill check — just Poison Trail ticks and last-hitting on both sides.","Level 2 is his: the Glaive recast knockup lands before you have any goo.","Level 3 evens out — Mega Adhesive grounds Aureate Rush, his only way in or out.","Levels 4-5 stay skill-decided while you farm and proxy for tempo.","Level 6 is a wash, but your Grievous Wounds fights his Glaive and ult heals.","At first item your poison itemization and level lead tilt the lane your way.","With 2+ items your unkillable kiting and Fling make you the stronger threat."]});
